    "title": "Evening camp June 8-10 offers skill-building, instruction and fun for grades 3-8 on the Canes' home field - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Joey Cooke ,\n5 hours ago The Coral Shores High School football program will host a three-day youth camp June 8-10, offering players in grades 3-8 an opportunity for skill development and instruction.\nThe camp runs from 5-7 p.m. each evening on the Coral Shores campus and is designed to combine fundamentals with a fun, team-oriented environment. The cost is $100, with payment accepted by cash or check made payable to the Coral Shores Athletic Booster Club.\nOrganizers said the camp is open to all experience levels and aims to introduce younger athletes to the Canes’ football culture while building basic skills ahead of the upcoming season.",
